{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mario-andreschak/FLUJO/pulls/803","id":4750356580,"node_id":"PR_kwDOOAFVPs8AAAABGySwZA","html_url":"https://github.com/mario-andreschak/FLUJO/pull/803","diff_url":"https://github.com/mario-andreschak/FLUJO/pull/803.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/mario-andreschak/FLUJO/pull/803.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mario-andreschak/FLUJO/issues/803","number":803,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Integrate bounded filesystem reads with protected tool results and worker export","user":{"login":"flujo-app","id":300233937,"node_id":"U_kgDOEeU00Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/300233937?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/flujo-app","html_url":"https://github.com/flujo-app","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/flujo-app/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/flujo-app/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/flujo-app/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/flujo-app/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/flujo-app/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/flujo-app/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/flujo-app/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/flujo-app/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/flujo-app/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Filesystem read_file previously admitted a pathname size, opened a separate media-header handle, then consumed an unbounded pathname readFile. A replacement or growing file could bypass that admission. This draft uses one read-only descriptor for metadata, media classification and bounded body consumption, while retaining the existing text/media thresholds and explicit text opt-outs. It carries the reviewed conversation-list, protected-tool-result and immutable-worker-export integration from #802. Tracks #563 and #611.\n\n- Admit exact bigint metadata on one read-only nonblocking descriptor. Fill and reuse a header of at most 512 bytes, read body chunks of at most 64 KiB, and consume at most the admitted length plus one growth sentinel. Reject shrinkage, growth and detectable identity/timestamp changes; close on successful reads and every failure path.\n- Preserve the 100000-byte bare-text threshold, 32 MiB media cap, pattern/range opt-outs, media detection and encoding, text/hash/range projection and batch behavior. Record the accepted byte count. Add 35 focused Jest cases without changing existing tests or their limits.\n- Retain #802's bounded conversation-list reads and workspace/file-identity summary caching, original protocol-error handling and exact final successful-result bindings, and immutable worker payload guards. Preserve the prior browser Preferences, conversation-preview and Persona lock observation changes from #788/#790/#793/#794/#795. The original worker export route remains inert for this main draft.\n\nSource provenance: frozen #802 bfefb35607bf11f1f2144efbcb61c053d2648000 -> e622ccfe948a5b39366d405e2a1366fb228c6d22; final tree dd5f5c47c8c17e45f7fe3bb690bb8352959fb413, base main 0be972ac7b748703d09e407ef96beba45ab17b2a. The additive two-file/four-hunk patch is the exact filesystem156 V2 successor. All 2871 whole Source objects are pinned, with 2869 unchanged from #802. Preserve all 62 historical and five component mappings, the prior conversation-list slice, nine main resolutions, 19 current oracle inputs and eight provider objects. The earlier ModelHandler successor remains explicit. Shared reader #258 and protected creation oracle #276 are unchanged.\n\nThe first filesystem156 Source proposal introduced BigInt literals incompatible with the unchanged ES2017 root typecheck. V2 replaces only those 13 literals with exact BigInt constructors, using decimal strings for large values. Independent forward/inverse byte and value comparisons preserve every other Source/test byte, all 35 cases, the ES2017/ES2022 configurations and existing scripts. V1, its static P1 finding and all oracle/refusal history remain immutable; no actual compiler failure was claimed.\n\nValidation: Root accepted the distinct V2 Source and reconstructed all four patch hunks and the projected tree. Engineering independently joined all 2871 whole blobs/modes, 576 raw trees, the external unsigned commit, original mappings and all retained input/config objects. Security reported five baseline witnesses and 54 synthetic candidate controls; their serialized observations match V1. Those controls were not replayed here. The 35 authored Jest cases, semantic typecheck and combined ordinary/native qualification remain UNRUN before the new draft's first automatic event; fresh exact-commit qualification is required. Prior acceptance does not transfer.\n\nLimits and retained failures: root confinement remains a non-atomic pre-operation check. Explicit text opt-outs still admit large files, and chunks plus concat can transiently hold roughly twice the admitted body; this patch adds no absolute text-memory cap or privileged-writer immutable-snapshot guarantee. The original high156 header sink is read-only, so this is not an insecure-creation claim. #802's original bfef/0d3e/tree717d/run37363422645 attempt1 native result remains FAILURE, with 47 new annotations, 72 open findings and 254 related URI/index limitations. Its original build/typecheck cancellations remain separate. Original #801 47new/74open, #800 49new/76open and #797 49new/78open failures, earlier component failures/cancellations and original OPEN records remain retained. No scanner/configuration/triage change, closure/count-cause/native-clearance claim, merge, deployment or grade acceptance is included.\n","created_at":"2026-10-05T20:23:06Z","updated_at":"2026-10-05T20:23:06Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"fcb821e2254f10495b872070ea1d462e93a8a9cd","assignees":[],"